ui: pinch-to-zoom on macOS (InputMagnify), Tester.ScrollWith and Tester.Magnify

A touchpad pinch on macOS (NSResponder magnifyWithEvent:) reached no
element: MyGo had no event for it, so an app's timeline or canvas could
zoom only with Cmd+scroll. The surface view now sends PointerMagnify with
NSEvent's magnification and the modifiers, and the runtime gives it, as
InputMagnify with Magnify (the change of scale: 1+Magnify is the factor),
to the innermost element under the pointer that handles its input, as it
does InputScroll; nothing zooms when none takes it. Other platforms send
none.

The Tester gets Magnify(x, y, m), and ScrollWith(mods, x, y, dx, dy):
Scroll sends no modifiers, so a test could not drive Cmd+wheel.

Test: TestMagnify.

